# Step 1 API — accounts, sessions, roles, audit
#
# Works with the VS Code REST Client and JetBrains HTTP Client. Stands in for
# Swagger UI until springdoc supports Spring Boot 4.
#
# Run in order: the OTP flow populates @accessToken and @refreshToken.
# In development the code is written to the backend log, not sent by SMS:
#   [DEV SMS] to=+976******33 body=418207 is your verification code...

@host = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{host}}/api/v1
@phone = 99112233
@adminEmail = admin@stay.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123!

### Health
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

###
# ─── Phone-first authentication ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is both registration and sign-in. An unknown number gets an account here;
# the account activates when it verifies its first code.

### Request a login code
POST {{api}}/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "locale": "mn"
}

### Verify the code and open a session (paste the code from the backend log)
# @name verifyOtp
POST {{api}}/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "code": "000000",
  "deviceLabel": "http-client"
}

@accessToken = {{verifyOtp.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{verifyOtp.response.body.refreshToken}}

### The signed-in account, including its role grants
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# ─── Email + password (secondary path) ─────────────────────────────────────────

### Register with email and password — returns a code challenge, not a session:
### the phone still has to be verified before first sign-in
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "88001122",
  "email": "guest@example.com",
  "password": "SuperSecret123",
  "fullName": "Bat Bold",
  "locale": "mn"
}

### Sign in with email and password
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}",
  "deviceLabel": "http-client"
}

@adminToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

###
# ─── Session lifecycle ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Rotate the refresh token. The old one dies here; presenting it again is
### treated as replay and ends every session for the user.
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Revoke one session. Other devices keep working.
POST {{api}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Start a password reset. The response is identical whether or not the number
### has an account, so this cannot be used to test for membership.
POST {{api}}/auth/password/forgot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}"
}

### Complete the reset. Signs every device out, since the old password may be known.
POST {{api}}/auth/password/reset
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "code": "000000",
  "newPassword": "BrandNewSecret123"
}

###
# ─── Own account ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Profile
GET {{api}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Partial update — null fields are left untouched. Phone is not editable here.
PATCH {{api}}/users/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "fullName": "Bat Bold",
  "email": "bat.bold@example.com",
  "locale": "en"
}

### Set or change the password. currentPassword is required only if one exists.
POST {{api}}/users/me/password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "newPassword": "AnotherSecret123"
}

###
# ─── Becoming a host ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Submitting grants nothing. A SUPER_ADMIN decides in the Step 4 approval queue.

### Apply as a house owner
POST {{api}}/users/me/host-applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "requestedRole": "HOUSE_OWNER",
  "note": "Two-bedroom apartment in Sukhbaatar district"
}

### Apply as a hotel — organizationName is required for this role
POST {{api}}/users/me/host-applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "requestedRole": "HOTEL_MANAGER",
  "organizationName": "Blue Sky Hotel LLC",
  "organizationRegistrationNo": "1234567",
  "note": "42 rooms, 4 room types"
}

### My applications
GET {{api}}/users/me/host-applications
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Withdraw a pending application
POST {{api}}/users/me/host-applications/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# ─── Super Admin ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below needs SUPER_ADMIN. Use {{adminToken}} from the login above.

### Paged user list, shaped for AG Grid
GET {{api}}/admin/users?page=0&size=25&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Search by phone, email or name fragment
GET {{api}}/admin/users?q=9911&page=0&size=25
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Filter by status and role
GET {{api}}/admin/users?status=ACTIVE&role=HOUSE_OWNER&page=0&size=25
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### One user
GET {{api}}/admin/users/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Suspend an account — also revokes all of its sessions
PATCH {{api}}/admin/users/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "status": "SUSPENDED",
  "reason": "Chargeback investigation"
}

### Set identity-verification state
PATCH {{api}}/admin/users/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/kyc-status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "kycStatus": "VERIFIED"
}

### Grant a platform-wide role — organizationId must be omitted
POST {{api}}/admin/users/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/roles
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "role": "HOUSE_OWNER"
}

### Grant a hotel-side role — organizationId is required
POST {{api}}/admin/users/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/roles
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "role": "HOTEL_MANAGER",
  "organizationId": "00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001"
}

### Revoke a role. The organization goes in the query string, because DELETE with
### a body is unreliable across proxies. Also ends the user's sessions.
DELETE {{api}}/admin/users/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/roles/HOUSE_OWNER
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Audit log, newest first
GET {{api}}/admin/audit-logs?page=0&size=50
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Audit log for one target
GET {{api}}/admin/audit-logs?targetId=00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Audit log filtered by action and time window
GET {{api}}/admin/audit-logs?action=USER_ROLE_GRANTED&from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
